In addition to what everyone else said, it should be noted that
your quest takes place outside the main dungeon-- you find
a special portal somewhere around dungeon level 14 or so to get there
(on the appropriate level, you will get a special message about your
 quest leader asking for your help).

>An unrelated quesiton -- is there a way to make unholy water without
>making my god angry (praying at a contra-aligned altar)? And does
>dipping scrolls in holy (unholy) water bless (curse) them or erase
>them? Or both -- do you end up with a blessed scroll of blank paper?
>

There are several ways to make unholy water w/o praying at a cross
aligned altar-- once you have one unholy water, you can make 
any ammount more by dipping several stacked potions of water into
the existing unholy water.  In order to get some initially, you
could be holding water when you get your inventory randomly cursed
by monsters that do that [arch liches, etc], or you can use the fact
that if you are confused and read a blessed scroll of remove curse,
all items in your main inventory have a 25% chance of being blessed
and a 25% chance of being cursed [so if I want to go this route, I 
generally find somewhere very safe- i.e. the Elbereth square
in Sokoboan with doors closed and locked- and name individual potions
of water so that they dont stack- then strip, and drop everything but
the water, get confused, and read the scroll. ]


>Finally (although I am sure I will have many other questions later) --
>how do you recognize Medusa level? Many statues? Oracle level has that
>already.
>

You can recognize Medusa's level by the fact that it has lots of water,
or if you have telepathy [which you should by then], by putting on your
blindfold/towel and looking to see if there is a green @, then
examining it to see if it is Medusa.


